+        "default": "pose=none - the identity. _translate stays Vector3.ZERO, _rotate_y 0.0, _scale_uniform 1.0, and the two new cells _shear and _perspective are both 0.0, so every branch added in this pass is skipped: the basis multiply is guarded on is_zero_approx(_shear), the corner divide on is_zero_approx(_perspective) or a standing projected cube, and the homogeneous row still evaluates to 0.00 0.00 0.00 1.00. _ready calls _apply_pose only when pose != none. apply_grid_config was a bare `pass` and now returns on its first line unless a `pose` key is present, so all 6 existing placements build the identical console and stand at the identity exactly as before.",
+        "was": "four @export knobs, all of them cabinet: finish, wear, unit_code and plinth_height. Nothing about the transform was reachable from a map, and apply_grid_config's whole body was `pass` - so every placement stood in its map showing the ONE case where the matrix says nothing: ones down the diagonal, zeros everywhere else, a cube sitting square, until a hand reached the slider pad. A console built to hold two co-equal languages for one state, only ever photographed holding the empty sentence.",
+        "note": "The bottom row was hard-coded 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0 in the values array, which made the gray row decoration - a fourth row that could only ever say the same thing is not a fourth row. `project` is the value that pays for it: Godot's Transform3D cannot hold a projective bottom row, so the divide is done on the eight corners (w = 1 + p*z, corner drawn at corner/w) and the twelve edges are re-seated and re-sized on the result, while the third cell of the gray row reads 6.00. The other five values are reachable through the state the sliders already drive, each set to a value inside the domain _compute_layout sized the case for - TRAVEL is the sliders' own extreme and SCALE_MAX is the sweep the bay width was derived from - so no pose can put the specimen through its own vitrine.",
