+        "still_note": "ONE AXIS, NOT TWO, and the second was declined on the evidence rule. The obvious companion - how much of the matrix is shown beside the cube, the `workings` question transform_composition_workbench owns - is 16 Label3D cells at pixel_size 0.0016 inside a metre-wide cabinet; hiding or revealing some of them moves a few hundred thin yellow pixels, which a still cannot measure, and a sheet of it would look finished and answer nothing. THE SAME ARITHMETIC IS WHY framing IS SET TO 0.72. The body is roughly 1.06 x 1.59 with a 0.60 plinth hanging below the origin, the two bays occupy y 0.44 to 0.78, and the AABB centre the sweep aims at sits near y 0.20 - down in the apron. At the default distance the cube is about 0.1 m in a 2 m frame and the axis would be measured almost entirely on background. 0.72 crops the cap and the plinth foot and roughly doubles the bays' share of the frame. If the critic still returns a low focus number, crop-recheck the right bay and the cell grid before believing INERT: scale, shear and project change the silhouette of the specimen outright, and all six change every glyph in all sixteen cells.",
